# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows with the common global `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every
# file to CRLF. The committed blobs are already LF, so CI on Linux was green while `make lint`
# failed on a Windows machine for all 30 files at once -- `prettier --check` defaults to
# `endOfLine: "lf"` and sees every line as changed. The failure looked like a repo-wide style
# violation and was purely a checkout artifact.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is the load-bearing part: `text=auto` alone still honours
# `core.autocrlf` for the working tree, which is exactly the setting that caused this.
# `text=auto` keeps git's binary detection, so images and other binaries are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
